title Tactical DDD · Processing Job / Attempt · 76282d3
package "Job business consistency grouping (interpretation)" $PROC {
 class Job <<principal root>> {
  id: UUID
  asset_id: UUID
  owner_id: UUID
  source: dict
  operations: list
  status: str
  current_attempt_id: UUID
  outputs: list
  deleted_at: datetime | None
 }
 class Attempt <<member entity>> {
  id: UUID
  job_id: UUID
  attempt_number: int
  state: str
  lease_token: UUID | None
  heartbeat_at: datetime | None
  lease_expires_at: datetime | None
  deadline_at: datetime | None
 }
 Job "1" *-left- "1..*" Attempt
}
class "processing.schemas.Output" as Output <<value DTO; JSON>> $PROC {
 kind: Literal[primary, hls_manifest]
 object_key: str
 media_type: str
 size_bytes: NonnegativeInt | None
 sha256: Digest | None
}
Job "1" *-right- "0..2" Output
note bottom of Job
  UNIQUE jobs.asset_id: at most 1 Job per Asset.
  current_attempt_id: 1 member (deferred FK).
  handle_command(): validate submit hash.
  _retry_locked(): failed -> new queued Attempt.
end note
note bottom of Attempt
  UNIQUE(job_id, attempt_number), number >= 1.
  lock_pair(): current; live(): state/token/times.
  finish(): 1 primary, optional HLS; attempt keys.
end note
legend bottom
  Job.asset_id / owner_id: Media identities; no cross-context FK. Source is validated dict data.
  Attempt is an entity with its own ID/history; Output is a mutable DTO stored as JSON values.
  Diamonds = Attempt history and owned output values; there is no Output table.
  Output 0..2 is the accepted V1 lifecycle bound; JSONB has no length CHECK.
  Cancellation updates independent Guard + Job together. Anaemic records; rules live in modules.
endlegend

@enduml
